# Hard constraints (every task)

These are expensive to get wrong even in planning. Full detail lives in
`AGENTS.md` and `docs/*` — this is the checklist, not a second source of truth.

## Product (`AGENTS.md`)

1. **Two roles only:** Owner and Broker. No admin / agency / team-member role.
2. **Core loop:** list → browse → request to represent → approve → auto pipeline.
   No manual re-entry of property data for brokers.
3. **Frontend-only repo.** Backend is `yesbroker-api` (separate). Data via HTTP.
4. **Deferred:** WhatsApp automation, payments, in-app chat, ratings, team UI,
   AI features, buyer accounts — flag, do not build.
5. **"YesBroker" is a placeholder name.** One config constant; do not scatter it.

## Market & UX

6. **India / Surat first.** INR as `₹85 L` / `₹1.25 Cr`. Dates `dd/mm/yyyy`.
   Phones `+91 …`. Never `en-US` / `USA` locale strings.
7. **360px Android-first.** Design the phone layout first; desktop is enhancement.
8. **Portals never mix.** Owner and broker routes do not import each other.
   Shared code → `components/layout/`, `components/shared/`, or `features/`.
   Users see one portal, never both.
9. **Default `noindex`** for auth and portal routes. Private client data.

## Owner ↔ broker UI parity (building owner now)

10. **Broker is the visual reference.** When building or changing an owner
    screen, open the closest broker equivalent first and match shell, spacing,
    typography, cards, filters, empty/loading/error patterns, and motion.
    Owner and broker must feel like one product, not two apps.
11. **Reuse shared chrome — do not fork.** Header, mobile nav, section nav,
    and other portal chrome live in `components/layout/` (already used by both
    shells). Page patterns that appear in both portals go in
    `components/shared/` or a shared `features/` module — never copy-paste a
    second design into `app/(role)/owner/`.
12. **Same tokens, same components.** Owner screens use the same
    `docs/DESIGN.md` tokens, type classes, and shared primitives as broker.
    Role-specific copy, nav items, and data only — not a separate look.

## Design & code shape

13. **Canvas is warm cream `#EFEAE0`, not white.** One green hue family only.
    `urgent` = deadline, `danger` = destructive — never decorative.
14. **Never edit `components/ui/`** (vendored shadcn). Wrap in `components/shared/`.
15. **Never bare `brokerId` / `ownerId`.** Use `brokerUserId` /
    `brokerProfileId` (and owner equivalents) — wrong id = wrong person's data.
16. **Format via `lib/format/`** (and shared display components). No inline
    price/phone/date formatting. `snake_case` only inside `lib/api/`.

If a request fights these, stop and ask or flag deferred scope.
